# Version bump / release

When the user asks to **bump the project version**, **release**, or similar (e.g. “update to 1.0.5”, “bump version”), do the **full release** end-to-end — do not stop after editing files or committing locally unless they explicitly say otherwise (e.g. “bump only, don’t push”).

## Required steps (in order)

1. **Changelog** — Move `[Unreleased]` notes in [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) into a new `## [X.Y.Z] — YYYY-MM-DD` section; leave empty Unreleased stubs; update compare links at the bottom.
2. **Package** — Set `version` in [`package.json`](package.json) and the root entries in [`package-lock.json`](package-lock.json).
3. **Memory** — Sync [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md): header version, **Versions** table (Package / Git tags / Memory doc), and a short memory changelog entry for `X.Y.Z`.
4. **Commit** — Stage those files (and any other intentional release edits) and commit with a message like `Release vX.Y.Z.`
5. **Tag** — Create annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` on that commit (match package version).
6. **Push** — `git push` the branch **and** the tag (`git push origin HEAD` and `git push origin vX.Y.Z`, or equivalent with tags).

Follow the repo git safety rules (no force-push to main/trunk, no `--no-verify`, no amending unless the usual amend conditions apply).

Product history and version table live in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) · [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md).
